 "title": "FT-PR-01 – Storage bullet overfilled during unloading (propane storage example)",
 "description": "Top event: a bullet T-1/T-2/T-3 is filled liquid-full during tanker unloading, so liquid propane reaches the relief valves PSV-11/21/31. Demand = unloading continues past the 85 % fill limit (gate G-006); protection = high-level alarm LAH with operator response and the high-high trip LAHH closing ROV-11/21/31 (gate G-002). As in the source design, both use the same level transmitter LT-11/21/31 – event BE-004 is a common cause (R-004). Gate G-002 is the overfill barrier of bow tie BT-PR-01 (threat T1). HAZOP N01-06; FMECA S01. Illustrative data from the toolkit's data library – replace with site / vendor data before use. Propane storage and dilution worked example (HAZOP HZ-EX-PR-001).",
